  "colorUsage": {
    "primary": "Hot pink is the ticket action surface (header Tickets, Choose your ticket, Continue to checkout); always pair with the ink --jk-primary-foreground.",
    "inlineLinks": "Use --jk-foreground with an underline on cream surfaces; on ink chrome, cream links gain a lime underline on hover and focus. Pink is not a universal link-text color.",
    "muted": "Use --jk-muted-foreground for secondary text such as genre lines, help text, and plan notes; keep it on background, card, or muted surfaces only, never on collage.",
    "border": "Decorative separators may use --jk-border; table rules, field outlines, and selected ticket borders use ink (cream in dark) at 2–3px. --jk-border-width is 2px; cards and bands use 3px rules.",
    "status": "Destructive, success, and warning always carry a text label. Clash notices use warning (tangerine), not destructive. Sold out is a word on a muted card, never a color alone and never a strikethrough price.",
    "charts": "The palette encodes stages and days only with a text label beside every mark; stage color is never the sole cue. Review adjacency on cream and ink before using lime or cream as a mark."
  }
